            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Hydrostatic pressure. When the soil under and around the foundation saturates, the water table rises and pushes water upward through the slab, through cracks, and most commonly through the cove joint where the floor meets the wall. The slab is not a waterproof membrane, so once pressure builds under it water finds every available path.",
